id: SCA-069
title: Reverse shell pattern detected
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .sh .bash .py .js .rb .php
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: /dev/tcp/
    message: Bash /dev/tcp reverse shell — connects back to attacker machine for interactive access.
  - regex: bash\s+-i\s+>&
    message: Bash interactive reverse shell — grants full remote access to attacker.
  - regex: nc\s+-[elp]|ncat\s+-[elp]
    message: Netcat listener/reverse shell — used to establish remote access in compromised packages.
  - regex: python.*socket.*connect.*subprocess
    message: Python socket reverse shell — creates network connection with subprocess execution.
  - regex: php.*fsockopen.*exec
    message: PHP reverse shell — establishes socket connection with command execution.
fix: Reverse shells are always malicious in application code. Remove immediately, rotate all credentials, and investigate how the code entered the repository.
